WEBVTT

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:05.950
>> Good morning, everyone.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:07.170
And welcome to our board

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:09.570
meeting of 9/15/2026. We are

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.470
going to begin our meeting as

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:13.800
we always do in a moment with a

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:14.860
moment of silence to be

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:15.670
followed by the Pledge of

00:00:15.670 --> 00:00:17.790
Allegiance. But before we all

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.150
rise for a moment of silence

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:20.330
for those who are able, I'm

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:21.570
going to ask my colleagues if

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.400
there's anything that they

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.480
would like to share with us or

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:25.540
anyone or things they would

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:26.490
like to keep in our thoughts

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:28.210
and prayers and I know a number

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:29.860
of us do so. Let me let me just

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:32.900
start with the couple

00:00:32.900 --> 00:00:33.140
first.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:34.880
And as the board knows, because

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:36.700
we all participated last

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:38.100
Friday, we mark the 25th

00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.590
anniversary of 9-1-1. And I

00:00:40.590 --> 00:00:43.180
want to just make sure that

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:45.120
folks keep in mind that 25

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:47.130
years is a long time. And as I

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.270
mentioned in my comments,

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:50.600
we have a lot of young people

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:51.720
recruits in our public safety

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.170
academy and in our public

00:00:53.170 --> 00:00:54.560
safety agencies that that

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:56.200
weren't even alive when 9.11

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.310
happened. And I think for us as

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:00.710
all reminder to never forget

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:03.390
that day. But also as I

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:05.790
reminded folks on Friday,

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:07.440
we have a lot of programs to

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:08.930
support our first responders

00:01:08.930 --> 00:01:10.620
and their health in particular

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:12.190
in this 25th anniversary.

00:01:12.190 --> 00:01:13.460
I appreciated that a lot of

00:01:13.460 --> 00:01:16.180
focus was on the health effects

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:17.880
and impacts on so many first

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:19.290
responders who responded that

00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:21.940
day and the health effects of

00:01:21.940 --> 00:01:23.210
the day-to-day work that they

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:24.500
do. And so we have great

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:26.130
programs in Fairfax County,

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:27.430
both for mental and physical

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:29.300
health for our first

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:30.540
responders. And that's one of

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:32.520
the reasons why we have such

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:33.610
great partners and public

00:01:33.610 --> 00:01:34.640
safety. But if we could

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:36.410
remember the victims from

00:01:36.410 --> 00:01:38.610
September, 11th, their families

00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:40.300
and our first responders on

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.700
this solemn 25th anniversary.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:45.370
And then secondly, we all know

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:46.610
in the community that we have
